# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization.
#
# ⛔ eol=lf is not a preference. The generators write their artifacts with
# newline='\n' and `--check` compares the BYTES, so a working tree checked out
# with CRLF makes every generated artifact read as DRIFTED. Git for Windows
# ships core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM config, so without eol=lf a fresh
# clone on Windows fails `npm run gen:check` on nine files before anyone has
# touched anything -- measured 2026-08-23. Nothing in this repository is a
# script that needs CRLF to run.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Merge drivers (tools/merge_driver.py; `python tools/merge_driver.py install`
# writes them into git config, and tools/merge_branch.py runs that on every
# merge). A path whose driver is not installed falls back to the ordinary text
# merge, so a fresh clone costs a conflict, never a wrong file.
#   grs-generated  rebuilt after the merge; keep a clean merge or ours
#   grs-ledger     generated blocks keep ours; hunks that only APPEND rows with
#                  disjoint ids are joined; anything else stays a conflict
#   union          one measurement per line, appended by the SessionStart hook
docs/spec/_assets/tbl-row-id-prefixes.md merge=grs-generated
docs/development-records/defects.md merge=grs-ledger
docs/development-records/fixed-defects.md merge=grs-ledger
docs/development-records/rulings.md merge=grs-ledger
docs/development-records/pending-decisions.md merge=grs-ledger
docs/development-records/measurements/stats.jsonl merge=union
